#!/usr/bin/env bash
# commit-msg — require a delegation trailer on every commit. Backlog D20, MEASUREMENT PHASE.
#
# WHY A HOOK AND NOT A RULE: the owner picked "measure first, then decide", and named the risk himself —
# "I stop writing it after a week". That is not a hypothetical here. "Writing a file into fleet-to-win/ is
# not sending it" was written 2026-07-28 and failed twice anyway. A rule that depends on remembering is not
# a mechanism, and this whole subsystem exists because of that difference.
#
# WHAT IT MEASURES: HARD DELEGATE says Claude does ONLY orchestration/dispatch. ~Half of recent commits are
# work done directly, but "no delegation trace" != "not delegated" — no trace convention existed, so BOTH
# readings of the rule survived the same evidence. That unfalsifiability is the actual defect. This makes
# the distinction recordable so the rule can be settled from data instead of from either of our impressions.
#
# ★ THE VALUES ARE DELIBERATELY FREE-TEXT. This is the MEASUREMENT phase — closing the carve-out list now
# would presuppose the answer we are trying to measure, and a list ending in "or other orchestration work"
# would pass every commit by construction (zero information). Let the real reasons accumulate, THEN decide
# which are legitimate.
#
# It REJECTS. It never auto-fills a trailer — a hook that invents the datum it is collecting is the
# dry-run-that-writes defect, and we have fixed two of those this week.
#
# Install: guard/hooks/install.sh   ·   Read the results: guard/delegation_tally.py
msg_file="$1"
msg=$(cat "$msg_file")

# Merges and reverts are mechanical, not authored work — nothing to attribute.
case "$msg" in
  "Merge "*|"Revert "*|"fixup!"*|"squash!"*) exit 0 ;;
esac

if printf '%s\n' "$msg" | grep -qE '^(Delegated-to|Claude-direct):[[:space:]]*[^[:space:]]'; then
  exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'EOF'

  ⛔ COMMIT REJECTED — no delegation trailer.

  Add exactly one line to the commit message:

      Delegated-to: <leg>            e.g. qwen3-coder via aider-edit · codex-terra · gemma4:26b
      Claude-direct: <why>           e.g. integration/wiring · guard code · owner comms · memory write

  This is the D20 MEASUREMENT phase (started 2026-08-03), not an enforced policy — the values are free
  text on purpose, so the real distribution decides the rule instead of us guessing it now.

  If a commit genuinely does not fit either, say so in the value rather than picking the closer one:
      Claude-direct: unclear — mixed, mostly reviewing a delegated draft
  An honest "unclear" is a datum. A tidied-up label is a fabricated one.

EOF
exit 1
